1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Empress Meishō (明正天皇 Meishō-tennō, January 9, 1624 – December 4, 1696) was the 109th Imperial ruler of Japan,[1] according to the traditional order of succession.[2] Her reign lasted from 1629 to 1643.[3]
2 CONT
2 CONT In the history of Japan, Meishō was the seventh of eight women to become empress regnant. The six who reigned before her were Suiko, Kōgyoku/Saimei, Jitō, Genmei, Genshō, and Kōken/Shōtoku. Her sole female successor was Go-Sakuram
2 CONC achi.[4] 
2 CONT
