1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tokugawa_Ieyasu '''Tokugawa Ieyasu''' 徳川家康] was the founder and first ''shōgun'' of the Tokugawa shogunate of Japan, which effectively ruled Japan from the Battle of Sekigahara in 160
2 CONC 0 until the Meiji Restoration in 1868. Ieyasu seized power in 1600, received appointment as ''shōgun'' in 1603, and abdicated from office in 1605, but remained in power until his death in 1616. His given name is sometimes spelled 
2 CONC '''Iyeyasu''', according to the historical pronunciation of the kana character ''he''. Ieyasu was posthumously enshrined at Nikkō Tōshō-gū with the name Tōshō Daigongen (東照大権現). He was one of the three unifiers of Japan, along wit
2 CONC h his former lord [https://www.geni.com/people/Oda-Nobunaga/6000000008261026303 Nobunaga] and [https://www.geni.com/people/Toyotomi-Hideyoshi/6000000001748966144 Toyotomi Hideyoshi].
2 CONT
