1 NOTE {geni:about_me} [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toyotomi_Hideyoshi '''Toyotomi Hideyoshi''' 豊臣秀吉] was a preeminent ''daimyō'', warrior, general, samurai, and politician of the Sengoku period who is regarded as Japan's second "great
2 CONC  unifier". He succeeded his former liege lord, [https://www.geni.com/people/Oda-Nobunaga/6000000008261026303 Oda Nobunaga], and brought an end to the Sengoku period. The period of his rule is often called the Momoyama period, name
2 CONC d after Hideyoshi's castle. After his death, his young son Hideyori was displaced by [https://www.geni.com/people/Tokugawa-Ieyasu/6000000001751290215 Tokugawa Ieyasu].
2 CONT
2 CONT Hideyoshi is noted for a number of cultural legacies, including the restriction that only members of the samurai class could bear arms. He financed the construction, restoration and rebuilding of many temples standing today in Kyo
2 CONC to.
2 CONT
2 CONT He is also known for ordering the Japanese invasions of Korea (1592–98).
2 CONT
2 CONT * From https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toyotomi_Hideyoshi, accessed 9 June 2019.
